+# Invoice guard admission proposal
+
+This packet is **UNAPPLIED**. Its exact parent is approved source-author
+`5f0f17dc9766411b260d5b53fd2db5a925adc80f`, sole child of checkpoint
+`f9335e5834fb06789585c4e59edd640447441bb7`. That author changes only the
+regular `100644` commercial draft SQL file: historical `da35d098…` becomes
+approved `e1c504f9…` through exact guard patch `45d2eeaf…`.
+
+The proposed checker and historical fixture readers remain payload copies. No
+canonical checker, historical assertion, test budget, worker count, SQL installation,
+grant, caller route or provider operation is changed by qualification. The existing
+historical SQL assertions still expect `da35d098…`; an explicitly verified fixture
+projection supplies those historical bytes while independently checking the actual
+approved guard source. This is development source admission, not genuine Auth or
+invoice issuance authority.
+
+`qualify.mjs` pins the packet metadata, patch and helper before importing executable
+bytes through a data URI. It checks every original tracked byte, mode and ancestor
+against the immutable 2,421-file parent frame. The protected targets must form one
+exact before or proposed-after phase; mixed phases and phase changes across import
+are denied. Only immutable Git metadata is cached. Packet and filesystem reads stay
+fresh before and after import and helper verification. The in-memory view overlays
+only the sealed payload targets; other paths use current repository bytes.
+
+Run only the new controls with the existing configuration:
+
+```sh
+npx vitest run tests/invoice-guard-admission-proposal.test.ts
+```
+
+The new controls cover exact SQL and historical caller admission, expected-hash
+rebinding, copied historical buffers, current-source withdrawal, coordinated unknown
+helper/launch substitution, protected companion edits, modes, symlink ancestors,
+wrong history, mixed frames, packet rebinding and changes across qualification
+boundaries. They do not replace the original suites.
+
+The sealed packet is evidence SHA256
+`e23de825623031192e5aff45a66c01860211e48f26e5c703cd0cc96375f5d8e5`,
+patch SHA256
+`2fc927fa37cb8da1ba4eccc8a4ea225ed847e07eadea496130ad61e6c09596cf`,
+and proposed helper SHA256
+`1d3438c34656e732c0352dab02477ea449ed4e4abd92714156c3ec62ff75e70a`.
+The patch changes ten paths, with 692 insertions and 13 deletions. The packet
+contains seventeen ordinary new files; canonical tracked bytes remain unchanged.
+
+Review identified coordinated helper/launch substitution, complete phase replacement
+across the import await, full-frame withdrawal during the helper's final reads, and
+fixture-adapter execution before authentication. The corrected helper binds its
+executing bytes; qualification preserves the captured phase and finishes with a
+fresh full-frame check. Eight proposed fixture headers now authenticate adapter
+bytes, regular mode and ancestors before data-URI evaluation. Fixed byte-edit
+recipes against immutable historical files avoid circular helper/adapter hashes.
+The direct altered-adapter marker did not execute in the new control.
+
+The final new controls passed **39/39**, with no failures or skips, and independently
+passed **39/39** on the same qualifier/test/packet bytes. The independent raw report
+SHA256 is `cbd38841fe27f0700112ea996a283346d4fffadae599eaad40f1068ba76a0c94`;
+the author's report SHA256 is
+`5eae6506777b739b88d353dc697505ca7251b236caa2725d40f3aec86c9845e1`.
+Scoped ESLint, Prettier and strict type checking passed. Independent review cleared
+the qualifier and new controls for offline preparation only.
+
+The final matching sealed-header disposable original six-suite run passed
+**90/90**, with no failures or skips, under the original four workers and 30-second
+budgets. Its raw report SHA256 is
+`2fb9fc5ee54511d31b66ca0a56f53fa02e834085224079800a978bf9fe9fd08e`.
+The three previously timed-out cases completed in 21.54s, 21.69s and 17.49s.
+
+An earlier run of the same sealed packet reported
+**87 PASS / 3 explicit 30-second TIMEOUT / 0 skipped**. Its raw report SHA256 is
+`9d7149cd3faa93ad31b7ae120027b22f25fb70e7662e2510a2630c55c5d527d0`.
+The native ten-caller plus thirty-four-issuance cases passed **44/44**, with no
+failures or skips; report SHA256
+`5e312cb72796390d782a0e12980b318fbeb849bff9387337f98a6b22c1877044`.
+Timeout cause remains undetermined. One bounded attempt on those same three identities passed under the original
+30-second configuration (20.07s, 20.21s and 16.19s); 37 other cases were filtered.
+Its raw report SHA256 is `31697477290cf0df85d119bbf0533b7274da89cb3350259be9cc69d119f45c77`.
+The final full 90-case run then passed as recorded above. Concurrent validation overlapped the failed
+run, but causation is not established. Earlier 90/90 development
+results belong to the preceding payload and do not establish final-source success.
+No full Foundation, timeout closure or operational acceptance is claimed.
+
+Source authoring, checker authoring, launch integration, commercial SQL/grants,
+genuine Auth/MFA, independent custody/recovery, D1–D3, A01–A12, merchant acceptance
+and real financial execution remain separate approvals. Release 1.0 remains NO-GO.
